# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bulwark .gitignore
#
# Read docs/git-workflow.md before touching this file. Every rule has a reason.
# Six-person team + heavy AI coding agents working in parallel — this file is a
# safety net, not decoration.
#
# THE TASK / LOG MODEL (full explanation in docs/git-workflow.md §1–§2):
#
#   tasks/  → temporary work orders from the project lead.  IGNORED by Git.
#             Distributed out-of-band when work is assigned. Never committed,
#             never force-added.
#
#   logs/   → permanent development & debugging history.     TRACKED by Git.
#             One file per feature/workstream, append-only, survives feature-
#             branch deletion. DO NOT add a rule that ignores logs/.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Temporary task files (work orders from the project lead) ────────────────
# The whole tasks/ directory is local-only. Task files are the scope fence for
# one feature; they are not project history, so they never enter Git.
# Do not `git add -f` a task file. Do not move task files into docs/.
/tasks/

# Belt-and-suspenders: a task file belongs in tasks/, never at the repo root.
/*-task.md

# NOTE: logs/ is intentionally NOT listed here. Development logs are tracked
# project history and live in `main`. See docs/git-workflow.md §6.


# ── Runtime data — NEVER commit ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# config/app.yaml `paths:` section. All auto-created on first startup.
# Contains uploads, OCR extraction output, generated artifacts, sandbox
# scratch, the SQLite DB, and the Chroma vector store. None of it is source.
/data/

# Stray SQLite files if a DB is ever opened outside data/db/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm


# ── Secrets / local config ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# There are currently NO secrets in Bulwark (zero external credentials — see
# docs/security.md). `.env.example` is the documented placeholder pattern and
# IS tracked. A real `.env` is not.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Per-machine config overrides. The 6 dev machines differ (OS / GPU / RAM —
# see docs/hardware.md). Shared config lives in config/*.yaml and IS tracked;
# a machine-specific override file is local-only.
/config/*.local.yaml
/config/local.yaml


# ── Python / backend ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/


# ── Node / frontend (React + Vite) ─────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
/frontend/dist/
/frontend/.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*


# ── Model weights — pulled locally, never vendored into the repo ────────────
# Ollama models live in ~/.ollama; PaddleOCR weights download on first run.
# These patterns only catch an accidental commit of a weight file.
*.gguf
*.onnx
*.safetensors
/models/


# ── Logs / temp ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This is runtime *.log output and scratch files — NOT the tracked dev logs
# under logs/, which are *.md and are committed on purpose.
*.log
/tmp/
*.tmp


# ── Editor / OS cruft ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
# If the team later wants to share a specific VS Code setting, un-ignore just
# that file, e.g.:  !/.vscode/extensions.json


# ── Claude Code / AI agent local state ─────────────────────────────────────
# Project-level .claude/settings.json (shared team config) IS tracked.
# Personal overrides are not.
.claude/settings.local.json
